{
  "interpretation": "The patch refactors app/db.py to return plain Python dictionaries instead of Pydantic models, aiming to reduce serialization overhead. Validation passed with 100% success rate and zero semantic mismatches, confirming API contract preservation. However, the runner rejected the change due to insufficient improvement. The candidate mean latency (0.5097 ms) was marginally lower than the parent (0.5130 ms), yielding a relative improvement of -0.0008 (a slight regression). Noise analysis shows the candidate has lower variance (CV 0.0148 vs 0.0245), suggesting more stable performance, but the absolute gain is negligible relative to the measurement noise. The hypothesis that Pydantic overhead dominates was not supported by the benchmark results; SQLite I/O or other bottlenecks likely remain the primary latency factors. The change is functionally correct but performance-neutral.",
  "limitations": [
    "Relative improvement is negative (-0.0008), indicating no performance gain.",
    "Improvement magnitude is smaller than observed noise variance.",
    "Only mean latency was optimized; p95 and max latencies showed mixed results.",
    "Does not address potential I/O or network bottlenecks dominating latency."
  ],
  "schema_version": 1
}
